# Review routing. GitHub requests these owners automatically on a pull request
# that touches a matching path. Later rules win, so the most sensitive paths are
# listed last.
#
# The point is not gatekeeping for its own sake. Every path below is one where a
# mistake is silent: it does not break a test, it changes what an attacker can
# reach.

* @d0mkaaa

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Delivery controls. Changing these changes what "passing" means, so they are
# reviewed even when the product change is trivial.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                       @d0mkaaa
/eslint.config.js               @d0mkaaa
/backend/.golangci.yml          @d0mkaaa
/package.json                   @d0mkaaa
/tools/                        @d0mkaaa
# A lockfile change is a supply-chain change. It is the diff a reviewer is
# most likely to skim and least able to reconstruct later.
/package-lock.json              @d0mkaaa
/src-tauri/Cargo.lock           @d0mkaaa
/backend/go.sum                 @d0mkaaa
/website/package-lock.json      @d0mkaaa
/admin/package-lock.json        @d0mkaaa
/account/package-lock.json      @d0mkaaa
/extensions/sesame/package-lock.json @d0mkaaa

